# Bloodforged Battle-Axe: "Whenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, create a token that's a copy of
# this Equipment." On turn 3 Bot1 attacks with an Ornithopter equipped with the Axe (2/2 flying) and an unequipped
# Llanowar Elves. Bot2 blocks the Ornithopter with its Guerrilla Gorilla (reach): the equipped creature deals combat
# damage to a creature, not a player, so no copy. The Elves are unblocked and deal 1 combat damage to Bot2 -- they are not
# the equipped creature, so again no copy. The Axe is still the only one: the one Bot1 cast. (The positive control is
# bloodforged-battle-axe-copies-itself-when-the-equipped-creature-connects.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Bloodforged Battle-Axe
Llanowar Elves
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Guerrilla Gorilla
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bloodforged Battle-Axe.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Bloodforged Battle-Axe.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Guerrilla Gorilla.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 2
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2; Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Guerrilla Gorilla > Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Graveyard = Guerrilla Gorilla
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 1
